{title: Blessed Be The Lord}
{subtitle: Psalms 68:19–20}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] |
| [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]chariots of God [Dm7]are twice ten thousand
[Eb]Thousands upon thousands in [Bb]the holy [F]place
[Bb]The Lord is among them in [Dm7]the sanctuary
[Eb]Sinai stands [F]firm in the [Bb]sacred space
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
You as[Eb]cended on high in your [F]might
You [Bb]led cap[F/A]tives in your [Gm]train
[Eb]You received gifts among [F]men
Even [Bb]from the rebel[F]lious
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Blessed be the Lord [Dm7]who daily bears our burdens
[Eb]The God of our [F]salvation is [Bb]here
Blessed be the Lord [Dm7]who daily bears our burdens
[Eb]The God of our [F]salvation is [Bb]near
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Our God is a God [Gm]who saves us truly
From the [Eb]Lord God comes es[Bb]cape from [F]death
He [Bb]crushes the heads of [Gm]his enemies
The [Eb]hairy crown of those in [F]guilt
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]I will bring them back from [Dm]Bashan high
[Eb]I will bring them back [Bb]from the depths of the [F]sea
The [Eb]Lord speaks and the [F]world is set [Bb]free
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Blessed be the Lord [Dm7]who daily bears our burdens
[Eb]The God of our [F]salvation
{end_of_verse}

